    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='DiD Calculation for Item Performance'>
      <repository-location id='DiDCalculationforItemPerformance' path='/t/Talabat/workbooks/tProxQCExclusiveDealsv2' revision='' site='Talabat' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_5' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='768' maxwidth='1366' minheight='768' minwidth='1366' preset-index='0' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='97916' id='3' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98828' x='586' y='1042'>
            <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97916' id='5' type-v2='text' w='98828' x='586' y='1042'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e96b1c' fontsize='13'>Difference-in-Differences for Item Performance</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Summary</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10'>In the absence of an experiment framework, to analyze if there was any quantity uplift (%) observed in the items that were purchased by tPro Users, we use a difference-in-differences approach between non-tPro v/s tPro users. To do this we compare the growth in quantity per user between the two groups (at an item level), this helps us control for the organic growth of the item that was discounted.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Analysis Methodology</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10'>Compare the tPro [Delta] Quantity per User v/s Non-tPro [Delta] Quantity per user to understand whether there was any estimated incremental growth in the items that were discounted for tPro users.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Item:</run>
                <run fontsize='10'> Lavazza Quality Rossa Coffee Nespresso</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>tPro Delta Quantity Per User = 37.58%</run>
                <run fontsize='10'> (Discounted + Organic/Seasonal Growth)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Non-tPro Delta Quantity Per User = 6.36%</run>
                <run fontsize='10'> (Organic/Seasonal Growth)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Difference in Differnce Increment  (DiD Increment) = 37.58 - 6.36 = 31.22%</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>The DiD Increment suggests that the item that was discounted is </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true'>estimated to have been purchased 31% more often </run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>now than earlier by the tPro customers.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e96b1c' fontsize='12'>Definitions</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Is tPro Customer (True/False) : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>Whether the customer was tPro or not when the order was being placed</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>SKU ID </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>and </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Item Name : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>Product SKU code and Product Name as seen on Catalog</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Campaign Duration (in Days) : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>The duration for which the item was on discount for tPro users continuously, this is regardless of the number of campaigns it was part of, the duration is merged if the item was repeated between campaigns</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Start Date (Date) : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>The date on which the item entered a tPro Exclusive Deals campaign</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Prefix - [PRE] : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>Based on the duration of the campaign, we select the same number of days before the item entered a tPro Exclusive Campaign. The end date of the pre-period is adjusted if the campaign is still running</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Prefix - [POST] : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>This is from the start of the campaign till the end of the campaign (the end of the campaign is [current date - 1] if the campaign is still running) </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Customer Count : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>Customer count is defined as the number of customer who have purchased at least one item in the given pre/post period</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Quantity : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>The total sold quantity of the item in the given pre/post period</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Quantity per user : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>[ Quantity / Customer Count ] </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>[DELTA] Quantity per user : </run>
                <run fontsize='10'>The % change in the quantity per user between the pre and post period</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='37' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='97916' id='36' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98828' x='586' y='1042'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97916' id='5' type-v2='text' w='98828' x='586' y='1042'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e96b1c' fontsize='13'>Difference-in-Differences for Item Performance</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Summary</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>In the absence of an experiment framework, to analyze if there was any quantity uplift (%) observed in the items that were purchased by tPro Users, we use a difference-in-differences approach between non-tPro v/s tPro users. To do this we compare the growth in quantity per user between the two groups (at an item level), this helps us control for the organic growth of the item that was discounted.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Analysis Methodology</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>Compare the tPro [Delta] Quantity per User v/s Non-tPro [Delta] Quantity per user to understand whether there was any estimated incremental growth in the items that were discounted for tPro users.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Item:</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'> Lavazza Quality Rossa Coffee Nespresso</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>tPro Delta Quantity Per User = 37.58%</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'> (Discounted + Organic/Seasonal Growth)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Non-tPro Delta Quantity Per User = 6.36%</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'> (Organic/Seasonal Growth)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Difference in Differnce Increment  (DiD Increment) = 37.58 - 6.36 = 31.22%</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>The DiD Increment suggests that the item that was discounted is </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true'>estimated to have been purchased 31% more often </run>
                    <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>now than earlier by the tPro customers.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e96b1c' fontsize='12'>Definitions</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Is tPro Customer (True/False) : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>Whether the customer was tPro or not when the order was being placed</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>SKU ID </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Item Name : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>Product SKU code and Product Name as seen on Catalog</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Campaign Duration (in Days) : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>The duration for which the item was on discount for tPro users continuously, this is regardless of the number of campaigns it was part of, the duration is merged if the item was repeated between campaigns</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Start Date (Date) : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>The date on which the item entered a tPro Exclusive Deals campaign</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Prefix - [PRE] : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>Based on the duration of the campaign, we select the same number of days before the item entered a tPro Exclusive Campaign. The end date of the pre-period is adjusted if the campaign is still running</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Prefix - [POST] : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>This is from the start of the campaign till the end of the campaign (the end of the campaign is [current date - 1] if the campaign is still running) </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Customer Count : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>Customer count is defined as the number of customer who have purchased at least one item in the given pre/post period</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Quantity : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>The total sold quantity of the item in the given pre/post period</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Quantity per user : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>[ Quantity / Customer Count ] </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>[DELTA] Quantity per user : </run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>The % change in the quantity per user between the pre and post period</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
